Figure 6: Macro accuracy score of few-shot cell type annotation on top 5 cell types.

SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE

Multi-panel line plot showing classification performance. Four panels are labeled Brain, Liver, HLCA, and Immune. The y-axis is ACC, and the shared x-axis is Number of cells per type. Two methods are compared in the legend: scDiff-Class in blue and scDiff-LLM in orange.

Main visible finding: scDiff-LLM generally matches or outperforms scDiff-Class across panels, especially for Brain and Immune, with accuracy increasing as the number of cells per type grows. Liver and HLCA show high, relatively similar performance between the two methods.
Figure 7: Macro F1 score of few-shot cell type annotation on top 5 cell types.

SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE

Multi-panel line plot comparing classification performance across datasets. Four panels are labeled Brain, Liver, HLCA, and Immune. The y-axis is F1 score, and the x-axis is Number of cells per type. Two methods are shown in the legend: scDiff-Class in blue and scDiff-LLM in orange.

The figure shows F1 score generally increasing with more cells per type. scDiff-LLM is usually equal to or higher than scDiff-Class, especially in Brain and Immune, while both methods perform similarly in Liver and HLCA.
